The agents of seed dispersal are:

1. **Wind** (e.g. cotton seed, tridax, Terminalia);
2. **Water** (e.g. coconut);
3. **Animals**, including birds, bats and man, which eat the fruits or carry hooked fruits on fur or clothes (e.g. mango, black jack);
4. **Explosive mechanism** (the plant itself, when the dry fruit bursts and throws out its seeds, e.g. pride of Barbados, balsam, cowpea pod).
